Z||000016||SpeedPhreak||12-16-1999||01:17 AM||||personally i like a harder feel in all my pedals i get more "feel" having to work them a little harder.<P>i still cant comment on the  & i atf because i still cant shift.  i have an 84 & think that it may be the clutch pedal that v8 archie talks about.  so i will put a new one in.  my dad came by on sunday (ex mechanic) & couldnt figure out what was wrong either.  we bled & bled & bled per v8 archie, gravity, & standard brake type bleeding.  he isnt sold on the atf but is curious to see how it turns out.  the rubber piece in the master cylinder got huge, i think that the atf may have had everything to do with that but i can still fit it in so im not worried yet.  so i will post when i get it going but its really starting to p*ss me off.....how hard would it be to retro fit a cable clutch system??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  now a more serious question to ponder...would it be possible to change the pivot point on the clutch pedal to allow for more travel?<P>n e wayz  merry christmas...check this out... im a mobile dj on the weekends, someone called our main office & offered  10 GRAND to play their party on new years & the dummy in the office turned it away... i think that i would have taken that job so i could afford to pay someone to fix me fiero & save my sanity  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by SpeedPhreak (edited 12-16-1999).]||||reg||9
Z||000017||Patrick||12-16-1999||02:13 AM||||<BR>SpeedPhreak, before you spend time trying to figure out how to increase pedal travel, make sure that there is actually more room for the master cylinder piston to travel in the cylinder. It's possible that it's being pushed to the end of it's travel as it is. <P>If anything, you may need to determine whether or not the slave piston is being moved the equivalent amount. If everything is working correctly, it should be. I've read that the slave piston only has to move 15/16 of an inch for the clutch to disengage properly.<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000018||SpeedPhreak||12-16-1999||02:42 AM||||Good point.  i am rather mechanically disfunctional when it comes to cars.  motorcycles on the other hand seem to come easy its kinda wierd u would think that it would cross over.  n e way. i can see what u mean now that u lay it out about the piston travel.  its just hard to get used to the clutch having zero free play at the bottom.  going from bike to van to fiero is a little wierd when the fiero has no free play & the others do.  no that i think about it there would probably be a lot more involved in adding some free play to the fiero.  the master cylinder, im assuming, would have to be engineered to let fluid back in after a set amount of return travel in order for that to work?  n e way it only takes a gear change or two to get used to it.||||reg||1
